{"uid":"progs/src/lxproc.c::_GNU_SOURCE","name":"_GNU_SOURCE","qualname":"_GNU_SOURCE","kind":"macro","file":"progs/src/lxproc.c","line":17,"end_line":17,"language":"c","signature":"#define _GNU_SOURCE","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"lxproc.c - foreground process-note probe (docs/spec/shell-fs.md, \"Process note\", and progs/minios_abi.h).","description":"Built twice from this one file: bin/lxproc carries the MiniOS process note\n(LXPROC_PROCESS_NOTE defined), bin/lxframe does not. Run bare in the\nforeground, the shell executes lxframe in its pid-0 exec frame and lxproc\nas an isolated process, and the probe reports what that gives it:\n\n  lxproc: exe /<path>         what readlink(\"/proc/self/exe\") answers\n  lxproc: fork ok             a forked child ran and was reaped (process)\n  lxproc: fork unavailable    fork answered ENOSYS (exec frame)\n  lxproc: fork FAIL <errno>   any other outcome\n\nExit code: 0 when every line is one of the expected outcomes, 1 otherwise.\nThe BDD scenario pins which fork line each variant prints.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"progs/src/lxproc.c","members":[],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
